  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_20541",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the treatment of various ovarian tumors through a chain of indications that ultimately connect it to Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary. The evidence suggests that Altretamine is used in the management of ovarian adenocarcinoma, which in turn is linked to Melphalan, a drug that is also used in the treatment of malignant germ cell tumors. This pathway implies a potential role for Altretamine in the treatment of a subset of ovarian tumors, particularly those classified under malignant dysgerminomatous or non-dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors. The shared use of Melphalan in these contexts suggests a possible mechanistic link, though the exact relationship remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Altretamine to be considered in the treatment of this tumor type, though further research is needed to establish a definitive mechanism of action.",
